WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.830
(audience cheering)
- We are celebrating

00:00:01.830 --> 00:00:03.131
50 years of hip hop.

00:00:03.131 --> 00:00:06.900
(upbeat music)
(audience cheering)

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:09.120
So to kick off, we have
a very special guest

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:10.710
in the Wayfair VIP lounge.

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:13.860
He is one of the most
in-demand DJs on the planet.

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:16.320
He spun at both Obama Inaugurations,

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:18.600
as well as at Jay-Z and Beyoncé's wedding,

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:19.433
not too shabby.

00:00:19.433 --> 00:00:20.930
Give it up for DJ Cassidy!

00:00:20.930 --> 00:00:23.129
(audience cheering)
(audience clapping)

00:00:23.129 --> 00:00:24.688
- Kelly!

00:00:24.688 --> 00:00:25.768
- [Kelly] What's up, man?

00:00:25.768 --> 00:00:27.737
- Oh, thank you for having me.

00:00:27.737 --> 00:00:29.880
- So, DJ Cassidy, you've
been a DJ for a long time,

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:32.670
and they say a DJ was credited
with starting hip hop.

00:00:32.670 --> 00:00:34.140
So can you tell us about that?

00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:37.200
- In 1973,

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:40.020
a young woman by the
name of Cindy Campbell

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:42.300
asked her brother, Clive Campbell,

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:45.390
to throw a back to school
party in the South Bronx.

00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:48.510
And that man's name was DJ Kool Herc.

00:00:48.510 --> 00:00:51.930
He got all his vinyl and he put 'em out,

00:00:51.930 --> 00:00:54.930
laid him out and said, "I'm
gonna create something new

00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:58.350
by playing the breaks of
these obscure records."

00:00:58.350 --> 00:01:00.990
And he played the
breakdowns of funk records,

00:01:00.990 --> 00:01:03.690
disco records, soul records, r&amp;b records,

00:01:03.690 --> 00:01:07.200
and those people dancing to
the breaks of these records

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:08.490
became break dancers.

00:01:08.490 --> 00:01:12.240
And this was the first hip hop
party of all time documented.

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:16.588
That's why this year we're
celebrating 50 years of hip hop.

00:01:16.588 --> 00:01:18.443
(audience clapping)
- That is a cool story!

00:01:19.470 --> 00:01:20.673
I didn't know that.

00:01:22.380 --> 00:01:23.970
I grew up in church and I feel like

00:01:23.970 --> 00:01:26.280
the first time I ever heard
a preacher really preach,

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:27.420
that's what it reminds me of.

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:28.740
Hip hop and rapping in general,

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:31.710
it reminds me of just
somebody that is so good

00:01:31.710 --> 00:01:32.700
at sharing their testimony,

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:35.490
like what's happening in their
lives and how it's evolved.

00:01:35.490 --> 00:01:37.500
It's almost like preaching
in a sense to me,

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:39.270
that's how I received it as a kid.

00:01:39.270 --> 00:01:40.938
- And it's a call and response, you know?

00:01:40.938 --> 00:01:42.338
- Yeah, it's really nice.
- Between the MC

00:01:42.338 --> 00:01:43.171
and the audience.

00:01:43.171 --> 00:01:45.007
For example, if I said to the audience,

00:01:45.007 --> 00:01:47.340
"When I say Kelly, you say Clarkson."

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:49.860
You would say, when I say Kelly, you say-

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:51.242
- [Audience] Clarkson!
- There you go.

00:01:51.242 --> 00:01:53.000
- Yeah, I like it!
- [DJ Cassidy] There you go.

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:54.910
- We didn't plan that, but
I just like hearing my name.

00:01:54.910 --> 00:01:56.490
(all laughing)

00:01:56.490 --> 00:01:58.770
Well, Cassidy, you've done a
ton of big shows and projects,

00:01:58.770 --> 00:02:00.600
so what do you have going on right now?

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:01.950
- So during The Pandemic,

00:02:01.950 --> 00:02:04.980
I created a series called "Pass the Mic",

00:02:04.980 --> 00:02:09.060
where I would invite iconic
hip hop stars onto my show

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:11.880
to sing along with their
most iconic records.

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:15.270
And after 10 episodes, the
show took the world by storm

00:02:15.270 --> 00:02:19.320
and featured 220 of the most legendary

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:21.840
hip hop and r&amp;b superstars of all time.

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:25.860
And this year, 2023, I'm taking
"Pass The Mic" on the road

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:30.000
with "Pass The Mic Live" to a
theater or an arena near you.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.820
So it's a very exciting year
for me, and for "Pass The Mic."

00:02:32.820 --> 00:02:34.260
And I'm gonna be passing the mic

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:37.347
to so many hip hop icons
throughout the year.

00:02:37.347 --> 00:02:38.550
(audience clapping)
- That's incredible, man.

00:02:38.550 --> 00:02:39.693
What a great idea.

